---
layout: null
---
{% comment %}
search.json - the index read by assets/js/search.js on /search/ (fetched once per visit).
2026-11-27 · new (site review: ~100 posts and no way to find one by word). wiki: http://localhost:3000/wiki/claude/blog_agent#l11
Every published doc of every collection (publish != false). text = the rendered body without HTML, cut to
250 words: that keeps the file small (~one screen of text per post) and still finds words from the body.
Every value goes through jsonify, so quotes, newlines and Vietnamese letters are escaped correctly.
Collections are rendered before pages in Jekyll 3, so d.content here is already HTML.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign sj_all = site.documents | where_exp: "d", "d.publish != false" -%}
[
{%- for d in sj_all %}
  {"title": {{ d.title | remove: "[🔥] - " | jsonify }}, "url": {{ d.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
   "short_description": {{ d.short_description | default: "" | jsonify }}, "result": {{ d.result | default: "" | jsonify }},
   "tags": {{ d.tags | jsonify }}, "board_parent": {{ d.board_parent | default: "" | jsonify }},
   "text": {{ d.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncatewords: 250 | jsonify }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
]
